        {
            "Section": "IT.IETESTCD",
            "Unnamed: 1": "IETESTCD",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the identifier of the inclusion criterion the subject did not meet or the exclusion criterion the subject met? [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 2,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": "CL.IETESTCD",
            "Unnamed: 7": 25,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "IETESTCD [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "IETESTCD [CDASH]\nIf the subject was not eligible, Record the identifying code for each criterion that was an exception. [completionInstructions]\nThis field is required to appear on the CRF, but may be null if there are no exceptions to the inclusion/exclusion criteria. The CRF should allow multiple exceptions to be recorded. See SDTMIG v3.2 Section 7.5.2 for assumptions regarding protocol versioning. Sponsors may provide a list of inclusion/ exclusion criteria and the unique identifying codes to the site. The list provided should be versioned/updated when the protocol changes and the criteria are changed. Sponsors should use sponsor-developed controlled terminology for IETESTCD. [implementationNotes]\nMaps directly to the SDTMIG variable listed in the column with the heading SDTMIG Target. [mappingInstructions]\nException Criterion Identifier [prompt]",
